dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/4 + [basic.def.odr]/5: naming `swap(declval<T &>(),
declval<T &>())' in an unevaluated operand (the decltype of a SFINAE
default template argument) instantiates the DECLARATION of swap<NoCopy>
only; the specialization is never odr-used, so its definition -- ill-formed
for a type with a deleted copy -- is not instantiated (g++/clang++ accept
the program).  The front end instantiates the definition anyway, fails on
the deleted copy and reports "dropped the body of function
'swap<tag-NoCopy>'" for a body no program can call.  The verification
result is right; the warning is spurious (audit residue item 12, round 162:
cpp11_is_swappable_unevaluated).
